{
  "pedal": "Boss NS-2 Noise Suppressor — reamps of the guitar DI dataset (mono: OUTPUT)",
  "comment": "The guitar DI dataset (captures/di/: noise, notes, dynamics, chords, chugs, funk, stabs, lead, neck; see tools/capture/README.md, Reamp takes) through the pedal: the main setting with every segment, the extra settings with the segments that show them. For the by-ear A/B and the numbers against NAM-X's model. INPUT from the interface, OUTPUT to input 2; SEND and RETURN empty. Threshold barely moves below 12:00 (the study: it opens at -68 dB re the guitar's peak at 9:00, -64 at 12:00), so the extra settings are at its top half: 5:00, where the model misses most (it closes ~1 s late), and 3:00, where it cuts a note's tail around -60 dB, with Decay at both ends. Clock positions: 7:00 = fully counter-clockwise, 5:00 = fully clockwise; 9:00 and 3:00 pointer horizontal. Takes ordered for the fewest knob turns: each step turns one knob.",
